================================================================================
PHASE 2 — SECTION LAYOUT NORMALIZATION
================================================================================
Fix Shelf as single owner of section spacing. Fix max-width inconsistencies.
Components adopt max-w-content token. Remove double-padding stacking.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SCOPE 2.1 — Shelf becomes sole vertical rhythm owner
Files: Shelf.tsx, page.tsx
Current state:
  - Shelf.tsx applies py-20 AND bg-brand-700 to every section
  - Inner components ALSO apply their own py-16 or py-20 (Featured: py-20, Dacs/IemsGallery/Accessories: py-16)
  - This creates 80px + 64px = 144px or 80px + 80px = 160px double-stacked padding
  - Shelf always applies bg-brand-700 even when children have their own bg (brand-900, brand-700)
---
Deliverable State:
  - Shelf.tsx: removes bg-brand-700 (sections own their own background)
  - Shelf.tsx: keeps py-20 as sole vertical rhythm
  - All inner component wrappers: remove their own py-* classes
  - page.tsx: no Shelf wrapper on Hero (Hero owns its own height)
In Scope:
  - Shelf.tsx: remove bg-brand-700 from the <section>
  - Featured.tsx inner wrapper: remove py-20 from mx-auto max-w-[1280px] div
  - IemsGallery.tsx inner wrapper: remove py-16 from mx-auto max-w-[1280px] div
  - Dacs.tsx inner wrapper: remove py-16 from mx-auto max-w-[1280px] div
  - Accessories.tsx inner wrapper: remove py-16 from mx-auto max-w-[1280px] div
  - NewestRelease.tsx: remove independent padding if present
Out of Scope:
  - Changing any card components
  - Changing carousel controls
  - Changing any section's internal grid/flex layout
Forbidden:
  - Adding new py-* values to inner wrappers
  - Changing Shelf's py-20 value (that is the system's vertical rhythm token)
  - Removing Shelf wrappers from page.tsx
---
